# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE BOARD-SIDE HASH DOES AND DOES NOT ESTABLISH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The hashes below are of the LOCAL files.  The gate session verified the
# uploaded copies by sha256 before configuring the PL, but that comparison was
# not written into the retained transcripts (00..03_*.txt).
#
# Re-hashing the board-side copies now yields POST-HOC CORROBORATION, NOT
# CLOSURE OF THE HISTORICAL CHAIN.  It shows that files with these hashes are
# present at that path today; it cannot show that these were the bytes the PL
# was configured from on 2026-08-17, because nothing in the retained record
# binds the configure step to a hash taken at that moment.  STRICT CLOSURE
# WOULD REQUIRE HASHING IMMEDIATELY BEFORE A REPEATED GATE RUN, in the same
# transcript as the configure and the vectors.
#
# The operational gate stands on its own (9/9 vectors, measured 125.0 MHz).
#
# Corroboration command — run from the workspace root in PowerShell.  Do not
# use a `| tee` pipeline in Git Bash: it reports the exit status of tee, so a
# failing board call can still look successful.
#
#   & .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe sw\board.py sh "set -eu; date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'; hostname; stat -c '%n|%s|%y' /home/xilinx/jupyter_notebooks/tme_probe125/tme_probe125.bit /home/xilinx/jupyter_notebooks/tme_probe125/tme_probe125.hwh; sha256sum /home/xilinx/jupyter_notebooks/tme_probe125/tme_probe125.bit /home/xilinx/jupyter_notebooks/tme_probe125/tme_probe125.hwh" 2>&1 |
#       Tee-Object -FilePath logs\board_125mhz_gate\04_artifact_checksums.txt
#
# The retained output is acceptable only if it contains BOTH expected hashes
# below AND the line `__EXIT__ 0`.  If the probe artifacts have since been
# removed from the board, do not back-fill: re-upload and re-run the gate.
#
# CORROBORATION OBTAINED 2026-08-18T05:39:08Z -> 04_artifact_checksums.txt
#   host pynq; both hashes match; both sizes match (4,045,690 / 395,091 B);
#   __EXIT__ 0 present.  Board-side mtimes are 2026-08-18 04:48:59.926 and
#   04:49:01.416 UTC, which fall inside the gate session window (the board had
#   booted at 04:42 UTC per 00_preexisting_state.txt and the PL was configured
#   after the upload per 01_load_and_clock.txt).
#
#   That timestamp agreement is consistent with these having been the
#   configured bytes, and it is still not proof: nothing in the retained record
#   binds the configure step to a hash taken at that moment, and an mtime is
#   not an integrity witness.  This remains POST-HOC CORROBORATION.  The
#   historical chain closes only by hashing immediately before a repeated gate
#   run, in the same transcript as the configure and the vectors.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
